From: overpressure <overpressure@pico4>
Subject: [PATCH] remoteproc: qcom_q6v5: a repeated handover is no error

PICO's SLPI firmware raises its handover bit (the vendor kernel's proxy
unvote) about five times a second for as long as it runs, and every edge
logged an error. The vendor kernel acts on the first proxy unvote and
ignores the rest; the handover is issued once here too, and a repeat is
logged at debug level only.
---
diff --git a/drivers/remoteproc/qcom_q6v5.c b/drivers/remoteproc/qcom_q6v5.c
index 58d5b85e58cd..8d0fa090b78c 100644
--- a/drivers/remoteproc/qcom_q6v5.c
+++ b/drivers/remoteproc/qcom_q6v5.c
@@ -165,7 +165,11 @@ static irqreturn_t q6v5_handover_interrupt(int irq, void *data)
 	struct qcom_q6v5 *q6v5 = data;
 
 	if (q6v5->handover_issued) {
-		dev_err(q6v5->dev, "Handover signaled, but it already happened\n");
+		/*
+		 * The PICO 4's SLPI raises its handover (proxy unvote) bit again about five
+		 * times a second while it runs; like the vendor kernel, take only the first.
+		 */
+		dev_dbg(q6v5->dev, "Handover signaled, but it already happened\n");
 		return IRQ_HANDLED;
 	}
 
